            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A propulsion system (20) for an aircraft having a nacelle (25) and a fuselage (23) is provided. The nacelle (25) has a gas flow path (66) and a nacelle interior region (67). The system (20) includes a compressor section (28), an intermittent IC engine (22), a turbine section (26), a fan (24a), and an IC cooling system (38). A first electric motor (56A) powers the compressor section (28). The compressor section (28) produces a flow of elevated pressure compressor air. The intermittent IC engine (22) selectively intakes the compressor air flow and produces an exhaust gas flow. The turbine section (26) powered by exhaust gas in turn powers a first electric generator (54A). The fan (24A) is driven by a second electric motor (56B). The IC engine cooling system (38) has a heat exchanger (40A) disposed within the gas flow path (66), coolant, coolant piping (42), and a pump (44). The heat exchanger (40A) is disposed in the nacelle (25).</p>
            </abstract>
